1. verify approved scope, acceptance criteria, and the exact candidate SHA;
2. require `publicationReady: true` from `npm run ci:prepublish` and deny any override request;
3. generate the PR title/body from the publication manifest and validate them locally;
4. publish the branch/PR, read the title/body back from GitHub, and validate the observed values with the same policy;
5. require GitHub's independent protected checks and review evidence;
6. after merge, select the exact CI artifact, verify its digest and attestation, and promote it unchanged to staging;
7. verify staging, then request the non-bypassable independent production approval;
8. promote the same artifact to production only after approval and verify production;
9. run the dedicated known-good rollback workflow, verify recovery, and record bounded evidence.

Local readiness never authorizes publication, and publication readiness never substitutes for external evidence. The production gate remains blocked until a real reviewer distinct from the deployment initiator is configured with repository access; no agent or owner self-review can replace it.
